# Testing

Write code that is testable.

## Architecture

- Keep business logic independent from the Android framework.
- Inject dependencies (constructor parameters, or Koin when wired) instead of building them inline.
- Avoid static/global mutable state.
- Keep ViewModels free of `Context`; pass what they need or use `AndroidViewModel` only when unavoidable.

## Prefer

- small functions
- deterministic code
- pure functions for calculations, formatting, filtering, validation

## Unit Testing

- Business logic should be unit testable without Robolectric.
- Avoid hidden dependencies (no singletons reached from inside a function body).
- Mock only external dependencies.
- Test the ViewModel through its public state and public entry points.

## Scope

This template ships no test suite. Do not scaffold a testing framework unless asked.

When asked for tests, place them in `app/src/test` (JVM) or `app/src/androidTest` (instrumented)
and add the test dependencies to `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.

## General

Generate code that is easy to maintain and verify.
